; M1e S1e.2.1 — a built-in predicate above its arity.
;
; The half of `CO-H1`'s class that is worse than the panic, and the half the
; review could not have guessed from the one instance it had: this file used
; to **load, compile, fire and exit 0**. `guard_holds` read `args[0]` and
; `args[1]` and dropped the rest, so a three-way equality was silently
; evaluated as a two-way one — a wrong answer with a success exit code, where
; the panic is at least loud.
;
; `A` and `B` are distinct, so a reader of this rule expects it not to fire.
; Before S1e.2.1 it fired.
(relation p T)
(relation q T)

(rule three-way-equality ()
  :match  (and (p ?x) (eq ?x A B))
  :assert (q ?x))
